<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Synthetic fixture: EVERY one of the ten structured-SIG component slots appears
  here under an element name this release does NOT recognize, and each carries a
  <Text> and a coded <Code>/<Qualifier> so that "absent, with no code and no
  text" is a real assertion rather than an assertion about an empty element.

  Nine of these names were recognized at the previous release and were removed
  because no committed artifact carries a field label denoting the component
  they populated; Frequency is the tenth removed name and also lands on the
  administration-timing slot. DoseDeliveryMethodModifier is the one name that
  was never recognized: the dose-delivery-method slot keeps its grounded name,
  so a neighbouring field label from the same published inventory is used to
  give that slot an unrecognized-name case too.

  Nothing here may decode: the whole <Sig> must read absent in all ten slots,
  hasStructuredData must be false, and no lossy warning may fire.
  Fully synthetic, no real PHI.
-->
